{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>They saw.</b> This verse is joined to the verses that follow after it, for they saw themselves in straits because Pharaoh said to them, 'You shall not diminish anything from your bricks, day by day.' They encountered Moses and Aaron and complained against them. The word 'them' is like 'themselves,' i.e., their own persons, and like it: 'the shepherds mistreated them' (Ezekiel 38:8), 'and he buried him in the valley' (Deuteronomy 34:6). Rabbi Judah ben Balaam said that it is like it: 'he shall bring him to the entrance of the Tent of Meeting' (Numbers 6:13), and in my opinion the priest orders him to be brought."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {0 "The rabbinic name is resolved by inference as Rabbi Judah ben Balaam, a known 11th-century French exegete frequently cited by Ibn Ezra."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:32:00.551596201Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}